Comments inside a signature are left out, so a `//` comment can't swallow the rest of the line and a block comment can't wrap it; a line break inside a template literal prints as `\n`, and comments inside a template's `${…}` are left out too while its text keeps its spaces. Every outline line stays one line.
== args
input/commented.ts
== file input/commented.ts
function count(
  a: number // the count
): void {}
function wrap(/* first
second */ x, y /* last */) {}
export function greet(message = `hello
world`) {}
function label(x = `${/* id */ y}  ${z}`) {}
